To mitigate this vulnerability, it is crucial to implement input validation and sanitization for the `name` parameter. One approach is to normalize the path using methods like `getCanonicalPath()` and ensure that the resulting path is within the intended directory. Additionally, you can strip or reject any path traversal sequences (`../`) from the `name` before constructing the `File` object. Adopting these practices will help prevent unauthorized file access and maintain the integrity of the file system. Furthermore, consider using libraries or APIs specifically designed to handle file extraction from archives securely, as they often include built-in protections against such vulnerabilities.


